# a program's word of a module word's name and arity, which another word of the module calls, is refused loudly: the
# module would run the program's word unseen (card rule-words-core); replacing a word no other one calls stays
'use math; norm(x) := 99; distance([3, 4], [0, 0])'	error	lib/math.warp's norm is hidden by the program's norm, which its distance would call
'use math; clamp(x) := 9; clamp(5)'	9
'use math; lerp(a, b, t) := 0; lerp(1, 2, 0.5)'	0
